https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=e58y60Ozhxs  (C5)  (Young John)

https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=kP3_yJIa_fY  (C2)  (Mature John)

Two versions here but with the same music and chords.  When John was younger he did the song in (C).  Later, as his voice became rougher he switched to (A).  To make both versions match the recordings I've done it here in (G), capo'd as indicated.  Young John does the final instrumental once; older John does it twice.  

TIP:  Of course John plays fingerstyle so to emulate this with a strum pattern the chords in upright brackets, the |C| and the |Bm| are strummed just once.  For the (D) - |Bm| - |D| don't come off the (D), just add your pinky to the 3rd string/3rd fret and play a quick three-note |Bm|, on-off.  The intro and first instrumental bridge is played as |C| - |C| - (G) but for the second bridge and the outro a second guitar comes in and there's an additional |C| - (G) played.  So instead of |C| - |C| - (G) it's |C| - |C| - (G),  |C| - (G).   
 
  
